	THE SOURCE FILES FOR EDUSYSTEM-30 SHOULD EACH BE ASSEMBLED
WITH 'EDU30.PA' WHICH PROVIDES THE SYSTEM I/O AND COMMUNICATIONS
AREA (EDU30.PA SHOULD ALSO BE ASSEMBLED SEPERATELY).  THE
BINARY FILES SHOULD THEN LOADED AND SAVED ONE AT A TIME WITH
STARTING ADDRESSS OF 07600 (EXCEPT FOR EDU30.SV WHICH
IS EDUSYSTEM-30 PROPER AND STARTS AT 07523).  THE SAVED FILES SHOULD
THEN BE MOVED TO CONTIGUOUS AREAS ON THE SYSTEM IN THE FOLLOWING
ORDER (WITH TEMPORARY (DUMMY) FILES WITH THE LENGTHS INDICATED):

EDU30 .SV  2
EDITOR.SV  9
TEMP1 .30 14
PASS1 .SV 10
TEMP2 .30 14
PASS2 .SV  7
PASS3 .SV 12
BATCH .SV  9 (BATCH MUST BE SAVED 'SAVE SYS BATCH 0-3577;7600'
		TO LEAVE ROOM FOR THE BATCH LOG)

	THE FILES MAY NOW BE COMBINED INTO ONE 'EDU30.SV' FILE
OR LEFT AS SEPERATE FILES (FOR DEBUGGING).

*** DO NOT CHANGE THE ORDER OF THE FILES OR INSERT OTHER FILES!! ***
